# All text files are stored AND CHECKED OUT with LF line endings, regardless
# of core.autocrlf on the developer's machine.
#
# This is not cosmetics. The package consists entirely of scripts that run on
# the router: the init script, generators, hotplug, the installer. A script
# with CRLF does not run at all — the kernel sees the interpreter as
# "/bin/sh\r" and answers "not found". With core.autocrlf=true and without
# this file any fresh checkout on Windows would turn LF into CRLF, and the
# local SDK build mounts exactly the working tree — i.e. broken scripts would
# end up in the package, and it could only be noticed on a live router.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must not be converted under any settings.
*.apk    binary
*.lmo    binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
